ENTRY            21214   20260311   20260827   20260827       2324
SUBENT        21214001   20260311   20260827   20260827       2324
BIB                 11         23
TITLE      Observation of two-photon decay in n-p capture
AUTHOR     (W.B.Dress, C.Guet, P.Perrin, P.D.Miller)
REFERENCE  (J,PRL,34,752,1975)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.34.752
INSTITUTE  (2FR ILL,2FR GRE,1USAORL)
FACILITY   (REAC,2FR ILL) ILL high flux reactor
SAMPLE     Distilled water (2 cm3) sealed in a bag of 0.006 mm
            thick Mylar placed inside a container made of 2 mm
            thick LiF enriched in 6Li.
METHOD     (COINC) Standard slow-fast coincidence arrangement
DETECTOR   (NAICR) Two 12 cm * 12 cm NaI(Tl) crystals
CORRECTION Corrected for
            - reactor power-level changes
            - dead-time problems in the conversion electronics
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) The following errors are taken into account:
            - counting statistics,
            - background subtraction,
            - uncertainties in calibration,
            - normalization,
            - detector efficiency.
HISTORY    (19791212C) CN.
           (19800115E)
           (20260311A) On. Major revision in 002.
ENDBIB              23
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           26
SUBENT        21214002   20260311   20260827   20260827       2324
BIB                  7         14
REACTION   (1-H-1(N,G)1-H-2,PAR,SIG,,SPA/MSC)
           Cross section for captures following emission of two
            gamma-rays in the energy ranges specified
INC-SPECT  Subthermal neutrons
MONITOR    (1-H-1(N,G)1-H-2,,SIG)
MONIT-REF  (21460002,A.E.Cox+,J,NP,74,497,1965)
COMMENT    *By compiler (2026-03-11):
           The authors say in p.754 left sig,abs=sig,1+sig,2,
            however, sig,2 is obtained by
            sig,2=sig,abs*(sig,2/sig,1).
           The value sig,abs=334.2 mb on p. 754 (right) is
            assumed to be a misprint for sig,1=334.2 mb.
STATUS     (TABLE,,W.B.Dress+,J,PRL,34,752,1975) Eq.(2)
HISTORY    (20260311A) On. REACTION updated.
